  "summary": "Investigated the done_script execution path and identified two root-cause concerns plus a concrete audit-trail proposal. First, `execute_done_script()` in `pipeline/scripts.py` runs the script in a daemon thread (`daemon=True`), which means the Python process can exit before the script finishes — this is likely why the script appeared not to execute. Second, there is zero feedback written back to the feature's history array when a done_script is triggered or completes; the only evidence is a timestamped log file in `.mad/logs/`, which is easy to miss. The fix should: (1) add a history entry like `{stage: 'DONE', note: 'Done script triggered: deploy-web-app'}` immediately before launching the script, (2) add a completion history entry `{stage: 'DONE', note: 'Done script completed: deploy-web-app'}` (or a failure entry with the error) once the background thread finishes, and (3) change the thread from `daemon=True` to `daemon=False` or use a proper join/atexit hook so the process cannot silently kill the running script. This gives a clear audit trail visible in both the TUI and WebUI item details without requiring users to dig through log files."
}
